nk":-0.013139104992603512,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":66.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07496295423163708,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0058099995,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"F5, Inc. provides multicloud application security and delivery solutions in the United States, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific region. The company's distributed cloud services enable its customers to deploy, secure, and operate applications in any architecture, from on-premises to the public cloud. It also offers unified, security, networking, and application management solutions, such as web app and API protection; multi-cloud networking; application delivery and deployment; domain name system; content delivery network; and application deployment and orchestration. In addition, the company provides application security and delivery products, including NGINX Plus; NGINX One Console; NGINX Ingress Controller; WAF for NGINX; BIG-IP Packaged Software; and BIG-IP Systems. Further, it provides a range of professional services, including maintenance, consulting, training, and other technical support services. The company sells its products to large enterprise businesses, public sector institutions, governments, and service providers through distributors, value-added resellers, managed service providers, systems integrators, and other indirect channel partners. It has partnerships with public cloud providers, such as Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform. The company was formerly known as F5 Networks, Inc. and changed its name to F5, Inc. in November 2021. F5, Inc. was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in Seattle, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Francois  Locoh-Donou | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["F5, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $17.7B market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 82% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $906M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.14316636277682598},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (39% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"F5 (NASDAQ:FFIV) EVP Chad Michael Whalen Sells 6,950 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/f5-nasdaqffiv-evp-chad-michael-whalen-sells-6950-shares-of-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793966938.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"F5 (NASDAQ:FFIV) EVP Thomas Dean Fountain Sells 9,387 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/f5-nasdaqffiv-evp-thomas-dean-fountain-sells-9387-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793964171.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"F5 (NASDAQ:FFIV) CFO Edward Cooper Werner Sells 599 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/f5-nasdaqffiv-cfo-edward-cooper-werner-sells-599-shares-of-stock