luation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 14%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $218 to $348 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks cheap against Technology peers: P/FCF 19.5 vs 25.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 18% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.1% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 9 covering analysts target $445 on average, 43% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 21% clears the cost of capital of 9.6% by 11pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.93).","It runs a 82% gross margin and converts 29% of revenue into free cash flow, or 22% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.37x.","ROE of 19% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 17.5% of revenue on R&D and 7.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $1.1B.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 5.7, in the safe zone).","Goodwill makes up 39% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.6% over 3 years, 5.6% over 5 years and 4.9% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 36% of profits supports about 7.6% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 8.6% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.06 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 65% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 11%.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (1.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 27, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (26 sales, net $8.1M sold).","It returns 2.8% a year to shareholders (2.8% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["CEO pay is $2.4M."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":77,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $231.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 49, gates 16/26)","ROIC 20.9% vs WACC 9.6%","FCF margin 29.4%","Net cash of $1.1B","Piotroski F-score 7/9"],"cons":["Trades 14% above fair value of $272"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":231.12,"vc":{"base":271.91,"base_src":"dcf","bear":217.78,"bull":347.62,"alt_median":189.55,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.4345,"dispersion":0.1369,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":26.7484,"ev_ebitda":16.351,"pfcf":25.4376,"pb":3.7763,"roic":0.0752,"gross_margin":0.4714,"fcf_margin":0.1275,"div_yield":0.0129}},"ticker":"FFIV","date":"2026-11-06"}